    "aboutPortrait": "images/APL02083-5 (1).jpg",
    "aboutHeading": "The Way I See",
    "aboutText": "I am drawn to the moments that ask for a second look.\n\nPhotography, to me, exists somewhere between precision and instinct—the balance of light, composition, and color meeting the unpredictability of a fleeting moment.\n\nI find beauty in contrast: the quiet and the dramatic, the familiar and the unexpected, the simplicity of a form and the depth hidden within it.\n\nWhether photographing a landscape, a person, or a machine, I search for the same thing: a sense of presence. An image that goes beyond what is seen and creates something that is felt.\n\nMy work is a study of light, form, and emotion—an exploration of the beauty that exists when we take the time to truly look.",
    "printsHeading": "Selected works, on paper.",
    "printsIntro": "A number of photographs from each collection are available as archival fine-art prints, produced in small runs through a partner. \n\nNot every image is available as a print. Where one is, you'll find a \"View Print Options\" link on that photograph's page, which will take you to Darkroom's site to review formats and place an order.",
    "printsNote": "Ordering, framing, and shipping are handled entirely by Darkroom. This site exists only to show my work.",
    "contactHeading": "Get in touch.",
    "contactIntro": "For commissions, exhibition inquiries, or general correspondence. A note here reaches me directly."
